; Tutorial_8_Check_Accessibility.inix -- checking a page, and who to tell.

[about]
Title=8 - Check Accessibility
Intro=Two accessibility engines over the page -- Deque's axe-core and IBM's Equal Access -- each writing a readable report, and Find Contacts for who to tell.
Setup=HomerView is open on a page to check.
Homework=Check one page with both engines and compare what each found.

[step]

Say=One want: what is wrong with a page's accessibility, and who to tell.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus Shift plus H opens the HomerView browser, or brings it back.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+H
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus A, A for Accessibility, runs Deque's axe-core over the page and opens a readable report.
Key=Alt+Shift+A
Hear=(the report's title, as a heading)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=It starts in plain words: how many problems, and that an automated tool finds roughly a third of them. Then the worst first, each with its WCAG criterion named and its level.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus E runs IBM's Equal Access instead, where your screen reader leaves that key free; otherwise Check Accessibility offers it, which folds Section 508 and EN 301 549 in with WCAG.
Key=Alt+Shift+E
Hear=(the IBM report's title, as a heading)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Use both; they disagree usefully. Then Alt plus Shift plus C, Find Contacts, answers who to tell: it looks on this page, the home page, and where accessibility statements usually live.
Key=Alt+Shift+C
Hear=(the contacts found, and where)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: reading a report of no problems as a clean bill of health. An automated check finds only some problems; a person using the page finds the rest.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Check with axe-core.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus A

[step]

Say=Check with Equal Access.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus E

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus C, Find Contacts, finds who to tell: email addresses, the accessibility statement, and contact forms.
Key=Alt+Shift+C
Hear=Contacts for this site
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Report Accessibility, from the Alternate Menu, tests the page and writes a report addressed to whoever publishes the site.
Key=Alt+F10
Hear=Alternate Menu
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type report, and Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=Report Accessibility
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The report is a page of its own, plain and polite, ready to send to the contact just found.
Key=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus Y, before testing, says how the page is built, which often explains a result: no headings, or a form with unlabelled fields.
Key=Alt+Shift+Y
Hear=0 headings, 112 links, 1 form
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=An automated test finds many problems but not all; the report says so, and lists what a person should still check.
Key=

[step]

Say=For a whole site, urlCheck, another Homer program, checks a list of pages and drafts a conformance report.
Key=

[step]

Say=Checking takes a minute, and a clear report makes a fix far more likely than a complaint.
Key=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus D closes a browser dialog that blocks the page, such as a cookie banner, before testing.
Key=Alt+Shift+D
Hear=Dialog dismissed
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus A again, after a site fixes its page, shows whether the fix worked.
Key=Alt+Shift+A
Hear=Check Accessibility dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, for now.
Key=Escape
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Who to tell.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus C
